PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED (2026-11-26, suspend-failure analysis). Hardening only: it is NOT a fix for the
failed_freeze count (no path was found where the re-freeze makes a task unfreezable or keeps it runnable).
A thread that sleeps in a freezable state that is not TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE (TASK_KILLABLE|TASK_FREEZABLE,
e.g. a vfork parent) is not woken by TWA_SIGNAL (include/linux/sched/signal.h:362-366: the wake is
wake_up_state(TASK_INTERRUPTIBLE), and only on the first TIF_NOTIFY_SIGNAL). Its work stays queued, and
every later resume queues one more (16 bytes + one module reference each) for as long as the app stays
frozen. Skip a thread that already has a notification pending.

--- a/drivers612/samsung-oneui/freecess/freecess_refreeze.c
+++ b/drivers612/samsung-oneui/freecess/freecess_refreeze.c
@@ -61,6 +61,9 @@ static long refreeze_walk(bool act)
 		escaped++;
 		if (!act)
 			continue;
+		/* an earlier walk's work is still queued (the sleep is not interruptible): do not pile up */
+		if (test_tsk_thread_flag(p, TIF_NOTIFY_SIGNAL) && task_work_pending(p))
+			continue;
 		work = kmalloc(sizeof(*work), GFP_ATOMIC);
 		if (!work)
 			continue;
